iders Realities, and Boston Despair With Joe House, Tom Pelissero, and Bill’s dad.", "refs": ["rss:8b690bce-bd12-11f1-ad9a-b35b39f27e90"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 231.29, "d": 7.26, "text": "The Ringer’s Bill Simmons is joined by Joe House to react to the Steelers-Browns 'TNF' matchup before making their Ringer 107 picks.", "refs": ["rss:8b690bce-bd12-11f1-ad9a-b35b39f27e90"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 238.85, "d": 4.52, "text": "Then, Tom Pelissero hops on to discuss six NFL topics heading into Week 4.", "refs": ["rss:8b690bce-bd12-11f1-ad9a-b35b39f27e90"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 243.67, "d": 8.96, "text": "Wednesday, from the All-In Podcast: Jake Paul and The Chainsmokers: Turning Fame into Funds, Jake Enters Politics? and Venture Bubble Signs.", "refs": ["yt:uzV45QvPKtU"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 252.93, "d": 11.09, "text": "Wednesday, from Moonshots with Peter Diamandis: Anthropic's Wet Lab, Artificial Wombs in 24 Months, and Scalable Gene Editing, Moonshots Live number 297.", "refs": ["yt:VHg3oX1ytYQ"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 264.32, "d": 14.5, "text": "The Mates sit down with Ben Lamm at Moonshots Live 2026 to discuss why we’re entering a biological singularity, from Anthropic’s move into biology and scalable gene editing to the possibility of artificial wombs within the next 24 months.", "refs": ["yt:VHg3oX1ytYQ"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 279.12, "d": 10.98, "text": "Wednesday, from Bill Simmons and The Ringer: NBA Lie Detectors, Duren’s Future, Tomlin’s TV Splash, and a 2026 Sports Media Check With Kirk Goldsberry and Bryan Curtis.", "refs": ["rss:379ff0bc-a65a-11f1-9855-932e7e7d39bb"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 290.4, "d": 10.09, "text": "The Ringer’s Bill Simmons is joined by Kirk Goldsberry to talk about the Jalen Duren contract drama in Detroit and the NBA rule changes before reacting to quotes from NBA media day.", "refs": ["rss:379ff0bc-a65a-11f1-9855-932e7e7d39bb"], "seg": "week"}, {"t": 300.79, "d": 5.28, "text": "Tuesday, from Jesse Michels: 16 Alien Bodies Crashed